<!--
  Two URLs, and that is not an oversight.

  The three case studies at /work/thalesgu/, /work/sacem-collab/ and
  /work/sconnect/ still carry SACEM's copy under their own titles. They are
  noindex, unlinked from the work section, and must stay out of here until
  each has content of its own — listing a page in a sitemap while telling
  crawlers not to index it is a contradiction, and the copy is the reason
  the noindex is there. Add a <url> block per page as each one is written.

  /404.html is never listed: it is served with a 404 status.
  /v1/ is never listed: it is an archive, and it is noindex.

  Like robots.txt, only a sitemap at the site root is useful — this does
  nothing at /v2/sitemap.xml and starts working at promotion. design.md §3.12

  changefreq and priority are deliberately absent. Google has ignored both
  for years, and the only honest lastmod is the day the page last changed.
-->
